# MABEL speaker + mic — a stable ALSA card id on ANY USB port.
#
# The JMTek/Solid State System USB sound-card dongle (VID:PID 0c76:1203, drives
# the 8 Ω / 5 W speaker pair + mic; replaced the MZ-631M bar 2026-07-27) is a
# single duplex card: hw:X,0 is BOTH the speaker and the mic. Unlike the wrist
# cams (identical twins that only their hub PORT can tell apart — see
# 99-mabel-wrist-cams.rules), this dongle has a unique VID:PID, so it is
# identified by WHAT it is, never by where it is plugged in. This rule pins its
# ALSA card id accordingly:
#
#     any port / any hub / any card index  ->  card id "MabelAudio"
#
# WHY BOTHER, given the bridge already resolves the card by VID:PID through
# sysfs (mabel_hw/drivers/audio.py: card_for_usb_id) and therefore works with or
# without this rule? Two edges the rule closes:
#   * ALSA derives the default id from the product string — here the maximally
#     generic "USB PnP Audio Device", which yields card id "Device". ANY other
#     generic USB audio widget can collide with that and get one of them
#     suffixed ("Device_1") — a stable, explicit id removes the collision.
#   * It makes the card addressable BY NAME from the shell for humans and for
#     tools that are not the bridge:
#         aplay   -D plughw:CARD=MabelAudio,DEV=0 tone.wav
#         arecord -D plughw:CARD=MabelAudio,DEV=0 -f S16_LE -r 16000 -c 1 x.wav
#         amixer  -c MabelAudio sset Speaker 70% unmute
#
# ⚠ The playback control on this card is 'Speaker' (the old bar's was 'PCM', and
# it BOOTED at 0% — aplay then returned 0 and played SILENCE). The bridge asserts
# the mixer on connect; if you test by hand, set the volume first or you may
# "prove" a working speaker is dead. The 'Mic' control also has a playback side
# (sidetone to the speaker) — leave that OFF or the mic feeds back.
#
# ⚠ ATTR{id} must be set on the CARD device (KERNEL=="card*"), not on a PCM or
# control node — udev silently ignores it elsewhere.
#
# After installing, tell the bridge the new name (or leave it: the VID:PID
# resolver finds the card whatever it is called):
#     MABEL_HW_AUDIO_CARD=MabelAudio
#     MABEL_HW_AUDIO_DEVICE_PLAYBACK=plughw:CARD=MabelAudio,DEV=0
#     MABEL_HW_AUDIO_DEVICE_CAPTURE=plughw:CARD=MabelAudio,DEV=0
#
# Install: sudo cp 99-mabel-audio.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/ && sudo udevadm control
#          --reload-rules && sudo udevadm trigger
# Verify:  cat /proc/asound/cards      (expect: "MabelAudio" on whatever index)
#          python3 experiments/exp_audio.py
SUBSYSTEM=="sound", KERNEL=="card*", ATTRS{idVendor}=="0c76", ATTRS{idProduct}=="1203", ATTR{id}="MabelAudio"
